\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. While shepherds watched their flocks by night,
\par All seated on the ground,
\par The angel of the Lord came down,
\par And glory shone around.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Fear not! said he; for mighty dread
\par Had seized their troubled mind:
\par Glad tidings of great joy I bring
\par To you and all mankind.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. To you, in David's town, this day
\par Is born, of David's line,
\par A Saviour, who is Christ the Lord;
\par And this shall be the sign:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The heavenly Babe you there shall find
\par To human view displayed,
\par All meanly wrapped in swaddling bands,
\par And in a manger laid.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thus spake the seraph; and forthwith
\par Appeared a shining throng
\par Of angels praising God, and thus
\par Addressed their joyful song:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. All glory be to God on high,
\par And to the earth be peace;
\par Good will henceforth from heaven to men
\par Begin and never cease! 
\par                             Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

